From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 06 Nov 2026 03:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AP: tell the ucode hook that a CAC started

The ubus object of a BSS does not exist while hostapd runs a CAC, and
the kernel sends no NL80211_RADAR_CAC_STARTED for a CAC that hostapd
starts, so nothing outside hostapd can see such a CAC start. Call a
ucode hook once the driver took the CAC. A CAC on a background radar
chain does not use the channel of the interface and stays out.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
+++ b/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
@@ -1203,6 +1203,8 @@ int hostapd_start_dfs_cac(struct hostapd
 		else
 			iface->cac_started = 1;
 		os_get_reltime(&iface->dfs_cac_start);
+		if (!radar_background)
+			hostapd_ucode_cac_start(iface);
 	}
 
 	return res;
